        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Greek-born philologist and Orientalist in Britain, Rajendralal Mitra\n- Roles: philologists, Orientalists, Greek scholars, Indologists\n- Concepts: Indian Philology, Indology, transtheism\n\nFacts:\n- A Greek-born philologist and Orientalist lived in Britain for most of his life.\n- The Greek-born philologist and Orientalist is considered one of the most important Greek scholars in Indian Philology.\n- The Greek-born philologist and Orientalist is considered important alongside another person who worked in Indology.\n- The person associated with Indology coined the term \"transtheism.\"\n- Rajendralal Mitra had the same profession as the person who coined the term \"transtheism.\"",
